cff-version: 1.2.0
title: kv-quant — KV-cache quantization quality cliffs, quantified
message: >-
  If you use this software, research artifacts, or the quantified quality-cliff
  findings, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Amman
    email: amman@users.noreply.github.com
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ammmanism/kv-quant"
url: "https://github.com/ammmanism/kv-quant/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  kv-quant is a research-grade implementation of quantized KV caching for LLM
  inference under provable correctness gates. Its v1.0.0 release quantifies
  the K/V asymmetry law: key-channel INT4 quantization collapses retrieval
  accuracy by ~20% regardless of context length (the INT4-K cliff), while
  value-channel INT4 stays within 1% of FP16 — a scoped decision matrix
  (K8V4 as the recommended operating point) backed entirely by committed,
  checksum-pinned CSV artifacts, Wilson-95%-CI uncertainty quantification,
  and a claims gate that rejects any uncited numeric statement in the docs.
keywords:
  - kv-cache
  - quantization
  - llm-inference
  - attention-sinks
  - gqa
  - triton
  - reproducibility
